SN Lines v1.1

Simple, quick and efficient method of adding a quick one-liner to your
system providing a little hint or help here and there.  Completely random
and loaded into clips, so it's lightning fast.  I've included my _Lines
file for some examples, but more than likely, you'll have to change them
to suit your system.  Actually, this could probably be used for other
things, too, like a quote system (if you lower the minimum add access)
and have people's saying popping up all the time.  Who knows?  The sky's
the limit on this little bugger.

Quick & Easy Installation:

 1  Place it somewhere.  (PFiles: would be good.)

 2  If you want the "add a line" feature all to yourself, go to the
    bottom of the "1; Maintenance" items in bbsmenu, otherwise go to
    the bottom of the "2; Available everywhere" or "3; Main prompt"
    items and add the following line:

    LADD  |{#0SN:SN_Lines ADD}

 3  Load up the 'ol bbstext in your favorite editor and jump to line
    #67 and add the following to the end:

    {#0SN:SN_Lines}

    In steps #2 and #3 above, modify the path to suit and remember,
    \ = CTRL-Y and { = CTRL-Q.

 4  Load up the file _Lines in your favorite editor and modify the
    lines to suit.  The FIRST line is the configuration line which
    determines the minimum access to READ and ADD.  Modify them to
    suit, but WARNING, do NOT change the format of this line.  It looks
    like this:

    CFG: 1 31 /* DON'T CHANGE THE FORMAT OF THIS LINE!  <minread> <minadd> */
     ^  ^ ^
     |  | |
     |  +-+-- These spaces MUST be there!
     |
     +------- This keyword MUST be there!

 5  Reload your bbstext/bbsmenu via CNet's Control Panel menu (option
    #3, "Text/menu reload  RAmiga-T" and you're all set!

(This sucker wasn't big enough to deserve it's own .guide, installer, icons,
help file, blah blah blah plus tax...)

